Why Is Demand Increasing
Minimally Invasive Surgery: Surgeons are increasingly adopting navigation technologies to improve precision, reduce procedural risks, and support faster patient recovery.
AI and Robotics Integration: Integration with robotic-assisted platforms and AI-driven analytics is improving surgical planning, instrument tracking, and intraoperative decision-making.
Advanced Imaging: Integration with MRI, CT, and other imaging technologies provides real-time anatomical visualization and improves accuracy during complex procedures.

Surgical Navigation Systems Watch: AI-Powered and Robotic Navigation
The market is shifting toward intelligent navigation platforms that combine imaging, tracking, robotics, and artificial intelligence. AI-enabled systems can support surgical path planning and risk assessment, while robotic integration provides more precise instrument positioning during complex neurological, spinal, orthopedic, and other procedures.

