Why This Market Matters
Surgical navigation systems are becoming an important component of modern operating rooms by helping surgeons visualize anatomy and accurately track instruments during complex procedures. The technology is particularly valuable in neurosurgery, spine surgery, and orthopedics, where millimeter-level precision can influence procedural outcomes. AI, robotics, portable systems, and advanced imaging are expanding the addressable market.

